      <abstract>    
        <para>
      &productname; can be deployed remotely over a network using the Preboot Execution Environment (PXE) of a target device. By using a PXE boot environment, administrators can automate the remote installation and initial configuration of the operating system through tools like Combustion or Ignition without requiring physical media.
      </para>
      <para><emphasis role="bold">Prerequisites</emphasis></para>
        <itemizedlist>
          <listitem><para>A properly configured DHCP server</para></listitem>
          <listitem><para>A properly configured PXE boot server. For details, refer to: <link os="sles"
                    xlink:href="https://documentation.suse.com/sles/16.1/html/SLES-PXE-server">PXE
                    server installation</link><link os="sles4sap"
                    xlink:href="https://documentation.suse.com/sles-sap/16.1/html/SAP-PXE-server">PXE
                    server installation</link>.</para></listitem>
        </itemizedlist>
        
      </abstract>
